[probes]
?p1 What is required to depend on Anyhow in no_std mode besides disabling the default "std" feature?
  = A global allocator is required.
  > README.md::"No-std support" #c52f3dc8d20d
?p2 What does the `backtrace!` macro expand to when `feature = "std"` is disabled?
  = None
  > src/backtrace.rs:15-19 #8cf3b162206f
?p3 What does Chain::new set as the initial ChainState?
  = ChainState::Linked with next set to Some(head).
  > src/chain.rs::new #87c2ee6783ff
?p4 Why does `Result::context` use pattern matching instead of `map_err`?
  = To save 2 useless frames off the captured backtrace in ext_context.
  > src/context.rs::context #f36af7f6ccb8
?p5 What is the capacity of the byte buffer used in `Buf` for formatting debug representations?
  = 40 bytes.
  > src/ensure.rs::Buf #4a5b381c47a4
?p6 What traits does __fancy_ensure import to support conditional debug formatting of operands?
  = BothDebug and NotBothDebug from $crate::__private.
  > src/ensure.rs:892 #47003f4166b3
?p7 What type of pointer does Error::construct store inside Error to erase the concrete type?
  = A thin pointer via Own<ErrorImpl> cast from Box<ErrorImpl<E>>.
  > src/error.rs::Error.construct #018b71bbe165
?p8 What happens to the backtrace when converting via reallocate_into_boxed_dyn_error_without_backtrace?
  = It is discarded.
  > src/error.rs:617-619 #1c7e5adc18e3
?p9 What does ErrorImpl::debug output when alternate formatting (f.alternate()) is enabled?
  = It returns the result of Debug::fmt(error, f).
  > src/fmt.rs::ErrorImpl.debug #dfe9d90dac0b
?p10 What constructor does Adhoc::new invoke to generate an Error?
  = Error::construct_from_adhoc(message, backtrace!())
  > src/kind.rs::Adhoc.new #a8a73a767218
?p11 What traits must a context type `C` implement to be passed to `context` or `with_context`?
  = Display + Send + Sync + 'static
  > src/lib.rs::Context.context #345f4a40e0bd
?p12 What does doc-mode `ensure!($cond)` return as the error message when called without a custom message or error?
  = A message constructed via `concat!("Condition failed: `", stringify!($cond), "`")`.
  > src/macros.rs:132-134 #727bb3d14c4e
?p13 Which compiler feature does src/nightly.rs enable under anyhow_build_probe?
  = error_generic_member_access
  > src/nightly.rs:5 #768689ae1608
?p14 What standard library method does Own::new use to obtain a NonNull pointer from a Box<T>?
  = Box::leak
  > src/ptr.rs::new #e46ede855974
?p15 What formatting trait does DisplayError<M>'s Debug implementation delegate to?
  = Display (via Display::fmt).
  > src/wrapper.rs:27 #00d202c92b7f
?p16 Which environment variable settings ensure only panics have backtraces, while errors do not?
  = RUST_BACKTRACE=1 and RUST_LIB_BACKTRACE=0.
  > README.md:86-87 #e8e36b2f9c5a
?p17 How is `Backtrace` declared in src/backtrace.rs when the `std` feature is not enabled?
  = As an empty enum: pub(crate) enum Backtrace {}
  > src/backtrace.rs::Backtrace #a2a5bc9272ef
?p18 What state does next_back transition a Chain into if it was currently Linked?
  = Buffered holding the remaining iterator.
  > src/chain.rs::DoubleEndedIterator.next_back #95c585d2e85c
?p19 How does `ContextError<C, Error>` retrieve its `StdError::source`?
  = Through `unsafe { crate::ErrorImpl::error(self.error.inner.by_ref()) }`.
  > src/context.rs:157 #5854e0dee432
?p20 Which specific characters cause `Buf::write_str` to return `Err(fmt::Error)`?
  = Spaces (b' ') and newlines (b'\n').
  > src/ensure.rs::Write.write_str #bd9dd04c4ac4
?p21 What helper function evaluates negation of the condition in __fallback_ensure?
  = $crate::__private::not
  > src/ensure.rs:914 #bdaf1d78d9bf
?p22 Why is ErrorImpl marked with #[repr(C)]?
  = To ensure that E remains in the final position.
  > src/error.rs::Some #bf9085671ef1
?p23 When Indented has no number set (None), how many spaces are prepended to the start of each line?
  = 4 spaces.
  > src/fmt.rs::write_str #60d458fbc0cc
?p24 What trait bound does TraitKind require for its generic type E?
  = Into<Error>
  > src/kind.rs:87 #7ecb203553be
?p25 What downcast targets are supported on an `anyhow::Error` after attaching context of type `C` onto an error of type `E`?
  = Either `C` or `E`.
  > src/lib.rs:527-528 #17c0642eb847
?p26 Why does the internal `__anyhow!` macro omit `must_use` compared to the public `anyhow!` macro?
  = Because it is used by other macros where the constructed value is already known to be used.
  > src/macros.rs:226-227 #44a44cf43c1e
?p27 What function is invoked internally by request_ref to extract a value from an Error?
  = error::request_ref::<T>(err)
  > src/nightly.rs::request_ref #e69698ecbe43
?p28 What method on Mut<'a, T> allows changing its lifetime parameter to another lifetime 'b?
  = extend
  > src/ptr.rs::extend #abaf71dc2b48
?p29 What traits must M implement for MessageError<M> to implement StdError?
  = Display + Debug + 'static
  > src/wrapper.rs:31 #86bde2ff4dc7
